WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.192
Hey, Dreamer here, and welcome to season three.

4
00:00:11.192 --> 00:00:16.784
We're starting on the AI tab: the instructions your world gives each job the AI does.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.034
Open the AI tab, then Story.

6
00:00:20.034 --> 00:00:25.863
This is the main narration job, the one that writes the story for every turn of the game.

7
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.304
Every job comes with Voyage's own sections, like items and how to use the narrator.

8
00:00:31.304 --> 00:00:34.198
Keep them as they are and Voyage plays normally.

9
00:00:34.198 --> 00:00:36.731
Reuse a section's name and you replace it,

10
00:00:36.731 --> 00:00:40.348
and deleting one doesn't stick, because Voyage puts it back.

11
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.180
Your world goes in the custom box, which is added on top.

12
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:49.577
Ours has what things cost, how long the show stays in a town, and a few rules about people.

13
00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:55.086
Story Memory squeezes old turns down into the summary the narrator reads.

14
00:00:55.086 --> 00:00:57.456
Its custom box is what it must never lose.

15
00:00:57.456 --> 00:01:00.560
For us that's whether Bramble's back, the show's money,

16
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.268
and what the player knows about the Gilt Circus.

17
00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:08.531
Initial Start writes the very first scene of a new game,

18
00:01:08.531 --> 00:01:12.051
and opening structure is how that scene gets built.

19
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:18.862
Our custom fixes a common slip: characters calling the player by name before anyone's told them it.

20
00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:22.914
Action Info runs before the narration.

21
00:01:22.914 --> 00:01:29.810
It judges whether an action is possible and how hard it is, and impact is how hard an attack lands.

22
00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:34.101
Our custom says what each success level means at the show.

23
00:01:34.101 --> 00:01:38.928
The levels themselves are fixed, so describe them, don't invent new ones.

24
00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:45.549
Character Background writes the player character's backstory and appearance in the creator.

25
00:01:45.549 --> 00:01:48.530
You can replace this whole prompt, but I'd leave it.

26
00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:55.294
Our custom just says every character is the show's newest act, with no act worked out yet.

27
00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:02.272
Conversation Starters are the two short openers offered when a chat with a character begins.

28
00:02:02.272 --> 00:02:05.361
The default keeps them short and tied to the scene.

29
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:10.165
Ours adds what fits a circus, and one thing never to raise.

30
00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:12.624
One rule of thumb.

31
00:02:12.624 --> 00:02:16.499
These boxes are for voice, tone and guidance the AI can interpret.

32
00:02:16.499 --> 00:02:20.199
Anything that must happen at a set moment belongs in a trigger.

33
00:02:20.199 --> 00:02:24.721
And put each rule in the right job, or it reaches the AI at the wrong moment.

34
00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:28.665
That's the story side of the AI tab.

35
00:02:28.665 --> 00:02:31.970
Our instructions are linked in the description.

36
00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:38.510
Next time, the people side: new characters, their details, what they want, and how they chat.

37
00:02:38.967 --> 00:02:42.915
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

